===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Of an item that is one of a pair, the other item in the pair.
# {{lb|en|geometry}} Of a [[regular]] [[polyhedron]] with ''V'' vertices and ''F'' faces, the regular polyhedron having ''F'' vertices and ''V'' faces.
#: {{ux|en|The octahedron is the '''dual''' of the cube.}}
# {{lb|en|grammar}} The [[dual number]].
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Of a [[vector]] in an [[inner product space]], the [[linear]] [[functional]] corresponding to taking the [[inner product]] with that vector. The set of all duals is a [[vector space]] called the [[dual space]].
# {{lb|en|wrestling}} A head-to-head [[match]] or [[meet]] between two teams, such as two high schools or colleges.
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2010-08-03|author=Kevin Revolinski|title=Insiders' Guide® to Madison, WI|publisher=Rowman & Littlefield|isbn=9780762766505|page=137
|text=Wrestling '''duals''' and meets take place at the Wisconsin Field House. There are no advance single event ticket sales.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2014-11-18|author=Mark Schultz|author2=David Thomas|title=Foxcatcher: The True Story of My Brother's Murder, John du Pont's Madness, and the Quest for Olympic Gold|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9780698188709
|text=But Dave agreed to participate in the Bulgarian '''dual''', and that trapped me into having to wrestle, too.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2023-10-19|author=Jason Norman|title=American Women in Amateur Wrestling, 2000-2022|publisher=McFarland|isbn=9781476684864|page=203
|text=Early in 2021, she became the first female to compete and win a match at the Ter-Hark Cup wrestling '''dual''', helping her squad to victory.}}

